esports culture and industry economics, so I gave it `entertainment` with `finance` as acceptable rather than forcing
one. `repo-page.html`'s extraction level is a judgment call (partial vs. full) since code-hosting pages usually have
real README prose but also heavy chrome. `cookie-interstitial.html` and `boilerplate-heavy.html` are both `partial` even
though a real article exists underneath, because the surrounding noise materially degrades what a naive extractor would
recover. Most importantly: I do **not** have the actual contents of the 6 pre-existing fixtures (`news-cricket-jsonld`,
`recipe-sourdough`, `wikipedia-catlinks`, `repo-page`, `spa-video-empty-article`, `injection-title`) — those 6 lines in
the goldset are inferred from filenames only, not from content per rule 1, and you should treat them as placeholders to
